-- title:
--   Principal ideals agreeing at all height-one primes are equal
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring which is an integral domain and Noetherian, and suppose every prime ideal $P$ of $A$ of height $1$ is principal as an $A$-submodule of $A$. Let $g,t \in A$ be nonzero. Assume that for every prime ideal $P$ of $A$ of height $1$, the images of the ideals $(g)$ and $(t)$ under the structure map $A \to A_P$ generate the same ideal of the localisation $A_P$ at $P$, i.e. $\mathrm{Ideal.map}$ of $\mathrm{span}\{g\}$ along $\mathrm{algebraMap}\ A\ (\mathrm{Localization.AtPrime}\ P)$ equals the corresponding extension of $\mathrm{span}\{t\}$. Then $(g) = (t)$ as ideals of $A$, that is, the principal ideals generated by the singletons $\{g\}$ and $\{t\}$ coincide. (Note that the hypothesis on localisations is stated for extensions of ideals, not for equality of the ideals $gA_P = tA_P$ in some other shape; and the principality hypothesis is quantified over all height-one primes of $A$, not only those containing $g$ or $t$.)
--
--   This is the commutative-algebra content of the statement that a Cartier divisor on a locally factorial scheme is determined by its behaviour in codimension one; it rests on Kaplansky's criterion that a Noetherian domain whose height-one primes are all principal is a unique factorisation domain. It is used in the construction of invertible modules on schemes, in [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible.exists_iso_invModule_prod_pow_of_zeroSchemeIdeal_support_disjoint`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible.exists_iso_invModule_prod_pow_of_zeroSchemeIdeal_support_disjoint).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Ideal_span_singleton_eq_span_singleton_of_forall_height_eq_one_map_eq.lean

